;; Reviewed 2026-10-10 (written by Claude, from the design, the MACRO
;; manual and the debugger runs; for the user's review). Why this is
;; right:
;; - A VAR record parameter takes its actual's type tag as a hidden
;;   longword right after the address (section 14, item 5), as on LLVM;
;;   the parameters after it move up a longword: Move's dx is at 12(AP),
;;   Grow's bx at 8 and its tag at 12, again at 16 and its tag at 20.
;; - The tag passed: a variable's, a field's or an element's is its
;;   static type's descriptor, by MOVAB (p, b, bx.lo and bx.hi,
;;   boxes[i], boxes[0].hi); Twice passes on its own, 8(AP), as LLVM
;;   passes a VAR record parameter's; pp^'s is its block's, the longword
;;   before the record: its address minus 4, then the longword there,
;;   SUBL3 and MOVL @-8(FP), into the list's own entry; pair, a
;;   VaxRecLib.Pair, passes VaxRecLib's descriptor,
;;   G^VAXRECLIB_PAIR_DJFN0SFL, .EXTERNAL.
;; - Box holds a pointer, owner, at 8: its descriptor's count is 1 and
;;   its offset 8. Grow's NEW(bx.owner) names VaxRecLib's NodeDesc
;;   descriptor; bx.owner's address is kept in R2, which Grow's mask
;;   saves, across the call. boxes[i] := b copies the pointer with the
;;   rest, MOVC3 #12.
;; - Nothing reads a tag yet: it is for IS, type guards, WITH and
;;   type-bound procedures. run-tags examines each one received.
;; - NEW calls rtl/vax's GarbageCollectedHeap.Allocate by its symbol,
;;   G^GARBAGECOLLECTEDHEAP_A_A8NV38EI, .EXTERNAL, where it called
;;   POC_NEW (Phase 16 step 4, section 15, proposal 9): the same
;;   argument list, the size and the tag, and the same result in R0.
;; - Its variables hold pointers, so it has a root table, L_ROOTS in
;;   POC_DATA: a link, which POC_ROOTS sets, the count, 6, and the
;;   address of each pointer (b.owner at b + 8, boxes[0].owner and
;;   boxes[1].owner at boxes + 8 and + 20, pp, and pair's two pointers
;;   at pair and pair + 4), flattened as a type descriptor's offsets
;;   are. The initializer registers it with POC_ROOTS before it calls
;;   its imports' initializers.
;; - The program allocates, so its start calls the collector's
;;   initializer, GARBAGECOLLECTEDHEAP_INIT, and then SetStackBase
;;   (GARBAGECOLLECTEDHEAP_S_EA118OLO) with its own FP, the base the
;;   collector scans the stack up to, before the module's initializer.
;; - The debugger runs link tools/vax-runtime-stub.mar, whose Allocate
;;   takes memory from LIB$GET_VM as POC_NEW did and never collects.
